(TIM-55 - the time and timer property words are reserved variable names,
 which the manual's Reserved Aliases section (LANGUAGE.md:4773-4779) never
 says. `duration` is shown here; hand-run, the same rejection covers
 `elapsed`, `running`, `timer`, `stopwatch`, `time`, `unix`, `hour`,
 `minute`, `day`, `month`, `year`, `wait`, `sleep`, `milliseconds`, `ms`
 and `current`, while `second`, `start`, `begin`, `stop`, `finish` and
 `end` are all accepted as names.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox TIM-55.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   error: Cannot use 'duration' as a variable name - it's a reserved keyword.
   (no binary produced; compile error)
)
a number called duration is 1.
print duration.
